<!--
Optional Openbox window rule for the dedicated session set up by
openbox-autostart.example: starts EasyEffects minimized instead of
popping its window on top of Chromium.

This goes inside the <applications>...</applications> section of
~/.config/openbox/rc.xml, not in the autostart script - Openbox reads
window rules from rc.xml, not from autostart. If you don't have a
personal rc.xml yet, Openbox is using your distro's default one (on
Fedora, /etc/xdg/openbox/rc.xml); copy that to
~/.config/openbox/rc.xml first, then add the rule below inside its
existing <applications> block.

The class value below matches what EasyEffects actually registers
(checked with `xprop WM_CLASS` while it was running) - it isn't
guessed from the package/app name.
-->

<application class="easyeffects">
  <iconic>yes</iconic>
</application>
